    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Gunnar Henderson** stands as our premier offensive anchor with a standout 83.29 efficiency score. His matchup against Melton (xERA 4.30) is bolstered significantly by a +16% park factor adjustment and a favorable platoon setup, allowing him to capitalize on his elite skill set in the two-hole. **Kyle Tucker** (70.33) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (67.94) round out our top-tier trio; both benefit from advantageous order positioning and stable matchups against Sproat and Keller, respectively, making them must-starts to solidify our HR and RBI production.\n\nThe decision to start **Andy Pages** (58.91) over potential alternatives was driven by his moderate platoon edge, narrowly edging out **Nasim Nunez** (57.85). While **Nasim Nunez** provides valuable speed utility in the utility slot\u2014crucial for our 5x5 scarcity focus\u2014his score was hampered by an eighth-order penalty. **Liam Hicks** (53.47) and **Miguel Vargas** (54.92) represent our \"marginal\" tier; **Liam Hicks** earns his spot via a +11% dynamic platoon bump and leadoff role, while **Miguel Vargas** remains a steady contributor despite a slightly tougher individual matchup against Ray. \n\nWe are currently managing a thin bench due to the ongoing absences of **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jacob Wilson**, all of whom remain sidelined on the IL. With **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** also out of the starting lineup, our depth is severely taxed. Consequently, we are proceeding with caution: the current lineup is optimized for maximum efficiency, but we are effectively capped by these injuries. Owners should monitor weather reports, as any late-game delays could disrupt our expected at-bat volume, particularly for **Brayan Rocchio**, whose efficiency score (47.05) is already pressurized by his placement in the nine-hole.",
